#ASSERT NOT ((`HSBC Revolution earns on` `HSBC Revolution` `a Cardholder at the SGD50,000 Deposits ADB threshold` `a month position this card does not read` `an insurance premium paid online`)'s `depends on the merchant indicator`)

-- (1) cl.4, by statement description rather than by MCC. cl.4 bullet 5 names
-- Paypal among "Payments on money payments/transfers". The statement line is
-- written the way a real one reads -- "PAYPAL *STEAM PURCHASE", not the bare
-- word -- because that is the case the first encoding of this clause got
-- WRONG: an exact-match test on the description would have answered this
-- transaction as earning. Layer 1 classifies the line as carrying the PayPal
-- family, and this rule tests the family.
GIVETH A Transaction
`a payment through Paypal` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`           IS "PayPal"
    `merchant`                IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`  IS 5999
    `transaction description` IS "PAYPAL *STEAM PURCHASE"
    `description patterns`    IS LIST PayPal
    `charge kind`             IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                  IS 30
    `currency`                IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`        IS YMD 2026 5 22
    `posting date`            IS YMD 2026 5 23
    `payment channel`         IS `Paid in a website or app`
    `credential`              IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`      IS `Flags online`
    `made in Singapore`       IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `HSBC Revolution` `a Cardholder with no Everyday Global Account deposits` `a month position this card does not read` `a payment through Paypal`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 0

-- cl.4 bullet 10's proviso, AS A RECORD OF ITS LOSS. MCC 9311 is row 44 of the
-- excluded table, so a tax payment earns nothing -- EXCEPT through the HSBC Tax
-- Payment Facility, which the bullet carves back in and which ought therefore
-- to fall to cl.8's base rate.
--
-- The two fixtures below differ only in their `transaction description`, and no
-- rule in this module reads a description any more, so THEY NOW ANSWER
-- IDENTICALLY. That is the regression recorded at cl.4 bullet 10: the domain
-- has no constructor for HSBC's Tax Payment Facility, so the carve-back cannot
-- be reached. Both fixtures are kept, and the assertion below pins their
-- sameness rather than deleting the evidence -- the day a constructor arrives,
-- that assertion is what will fail and say so.
GIVETH A Transaction
`a tax payment at a government portal` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`           IS "IRAS"
    `merchant`                IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`  IS 9311
    `transaction description` IS "IRAS TAX PAYMENT SG"
    `description patterns`    IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`             IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                  IS 1_000
    `currency`                IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`        IS YMD 2026 5 25
    `posting date`            IS YMD 2026 5 26
    `payment channel`         IS `Paid in a website or app`
    `credential`              IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`      IS `Flags online`
    `made in Singapore`       IS TRUE

GIVETH A Transaction
`a tax payment through the HSBC Tax Payment Facility` MEANS Transaction WITH
    `merchant name`           IS "IRAS"
    `merchant`                IS `Another merchant`
    `merchant category code`  IS 9311
    `transaction description` IS "HSBC Tax Payment Facility"
    `description patterns`    IS EMPTY
    `charge kind`             IS `Retail purchase`
    `amount`                  IS 1_000
    `currency`                IS "SGD"
    `posted in a foreign currency` IS FALSE
    `transaction date`        IS YMD 2026 5 25
    `posting date`            IS YMD 2026 5 26
    `payment channel`         IS `Paid in a website or app`
    `credential`              IS `The physical card`
    `merchant indicator`      IS `Flags online`
    `made in Singapore`       IS TRUE

#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `HSBC Revolution` `a Cardholder with no Everyday Global Account deposits` `a month position this card does not read` `a tax payment at a government portal`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 0
-- THE CARVE-BACK IS UNREACHABLE. This assertion used to read EQUALS 1, and it
-- is the one place in this module where the encoding is known to disagree with
-- the document. Not a caveat: a failing case, pinned so it stays visible.
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `HSBC Revolution` `a Cardholder with no Everyday Global Account deposits` `a month position this card does not read` `a tax payment through the HSBC Tax Payment Facility`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `HSBC Revolution` `a Cardholder with no Everyday Global Account deposits` `a month position this card does not read` `a tax payment through the HSBC Tax Payment Facility`)'s `points per dollar` EQUALS (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `HSBC Revolution` `a Cardholder with no Everyday Global Account deposits` `a month position this card does not read` `a tax payment at a government portal`)'s `points per dollar`

